---
import { site } from "../../site";
---

<section class="wrap hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="hero__copy">
    <p class="meta home-eyebrow">00 / {site.role} · {site.location}</p>
    <h1 id="hero-title">Gabriel<br />Kimutai</h1>
    <p class="hero__lede">
      I work on backend services, Android clients, and the networking between
      them. Right now I'm designing a binary protocol from the header bytes up,
      which is slower, but I understand it better for it.
    </p>
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#work">Selected work</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/writing/">Writing</a>
      <a class="btn" href={site.github} rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero__art">
    <img
      src="/images/hero.png"
      alt="Engraved illustration of a small figure standing beneath a vast flower made of intertwined bodies"
      width="1839"
      height="2400"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap" aria-label="Current status">
  <dl class="status">
    <div>
      <dt class="meta">Now</dt>
      <dd>Full-stack developer at Innovative Tech Labs</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt class="meta">Building</dt>
      <dd><a href="/work/heimdall/">Heimdall</a></dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt class="meta">Reading</dt>
      <dd>Protocol specs</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>

<figure class="wrap figure">
  <img
    src="/images/figure-01.jpg"
    alt="Wide monochrome line engraving: a winged-hatted messenger with a caduceus stands over a crowd of reaching figures, with a man gazing skyward on the left and children at the lower right"
    width="2000"
    height="1000"
    loading="lazy"
  />
  <figcaption class="meta">
    Fig. 01 — Local discovery and control path. An Android client finds a
    Heimdall daemon over mDNS, then talks to it through an authenticated
    protocol to manage system, process and network capabilities.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
